ight like for females it's like they  would like  say like oh you're fat you kind of try  to humiliate you  before it's mail it's like okay do like  20 push-ups right now can trainees have  social media accounts this is a funny  one okay technically  no but i had one as long as they don't  find it it's fine i was not allowed to  have social media  i remember my current instagram i  deleted  all of the pictures can k-pop trainees  date i  remember part in my contract that said  like you know i can't have a boyfriend  which is  you know standard it's mostly forbidden  i've known people who've like dated the  like male trainees in their company  and that didn't end well the male  trainee was like fired how much do  kpop trainees get paid i got paid zero  bucks made absolutely nothing  my company at that time i paid for my  housing they paid for my food i had an  allowance i had  pretty much my life handed to me how  kpop trainees work is that like you  dance you sing  and then like obviously the studio  there's like a renting fee and all that  but the company pays for it because  technically they're investing in you  like when you debut hopefully and then  hopefully you get make a lot of money  you have to pay back the company  how do you go from training to idle well  takes a heck of a lot of practice  usually the company maybe has like 20 30  girls and then every month there's like  a monthly exam  and then they cut like a few girls each  month you have to be able to  withstand all of the companies like  demands  rules schedules you have to be okay with  not being able to see your family  and then usually right before a debut i  think a lot of them  would have like free concerts where like  trainees like travel around and like  give free concerts  just kind of like to build a fan base  you have to be okay with having your  privacy  invaded 24 7. in the recent years  ever since like produce 101 i think a  big thing was like these competition  shows where you can like 